From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:27:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 203/210] codecparsers: Add AVS1/AVS+ and AVS2 parsers

Add parsers for the start code units, sequence headers and picture
headers of AVS1 (GB/T 20090.2) and AVS+ (GY/T 257.1) streams, and of
AVS2 (GB/T 33475.2) streams, for stateless decoders.

The headers are read without the two stuffing bits that follow two zero
bytes in front of a 0x02 byte (pseudo start code method), which both
standards use. For AVS1, streams of the pre-final revision of the
standard without the marker bit after time_code are told apart from the
picture header values. For AVS2, the reference configuration set of
each picture is resolved from the sequence header, the weighting
quantization matrices that apply to a picture are resolved from the
default, sequence or picture header matrices or parameters (section
9.2.4), and the adaptive loop filter parameters give the filter of each
of the 16 regions.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
